  48:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h **** /**
  49:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * Public function mbedtls_pk_ec() can be used to get direct access to the
  50:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * wrapped ecp_keypair structure pointed to the pk_ctx. However this is not
  51:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * ideal because it bypasses the PK module on the control of its internal
  52:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * structure (pk_context) fields.
  53:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * For backward compatibility we keep mbedtls_pk_ec() when ECP_C is defined, but
  54:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * we provide 2 very similar functions when only ECP_LIGHT is enabled and not
  55:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * ECP_C.
  56:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * These variants embed the "ro" or "rw" keywords in their name to make the
  57:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * usage of the returned pointer explicit. Of course the returned value is
  58:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  * const or non-const accordingly.
  59:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/pk_internal.h ****  */
